spec.section:
## Card contract

`cards.json` is normative for this package. Every card has:

- a concrete record key and record type;
- at least two expected field/value predicates (the checker rejects an id-only
  assertion);
- an executable/procedural command and a concrete evidence query;
- a `status` of `planned` or `run`, plus a UTC date and commit/image marker;
- an explicit distinction between semantic, authorization, recovery, owner,
  and performance evidence.

The event cards `T-W1` through `T-W11` cover every NEW event in VOL-C §4.
`T-ACC-03` is the manager fan-out card: it cites `evt-w3-director-manager`,
whose body names `assigner: director`, `assignee: mgr-infra`, and `kind: task`.
It does not cite W1; W1 is only the VP objective opening event.
